2. 🏗️ Scalability & Architectural Flaws
These are the "bottlenecks" that will cause the site to crash or become extremely slow once you have real traffic.

"Download-All" Query Pattern (Critical Performance Flaw):
In productController.js and adminController.js, you are fetching all products or users and then filtering them in JavaScript (e.g., snapshot.docs.map(...) then .filter(...)).
The Problem: If you have 5,000 products, your server downloads 5,000 documents from Firestore for every search request. This is expensive (Firestore costs) and slow (latency).
Fix: Use Firestore queries (where, limit, orderBy) and implement a search indexer like Algolia or ElasticSearch for text searching.
Websocket Limitations:
realtimeHub.js uses an in-memory wsServer. This works on a single server, but if you deploy to a platform that scales horizontally (like Render or Vercel), users on Server A won't see events from Server B.
Fix: Use Redis Pub/Sub to synchronize WebSocket events across multiple server instances.
No Database Indexing Strategy:
Firestore requires composite indexes for complex queries (multiple where or where + orderBy). Your code (e.g., getMyOrders) sorts client-side because of this.
Fix: Explicitly define and deploy Firestore indexes.json.
3. 🛠️ Required Production Improvements
To make this a "Real-Time, Real-World" project, the following features are missing:

Production Image Handling: While you use Cloudinary, you should implement Responsive Image sets (Srcset) and Lazy Loading on the frontend to improve Core Web Vitals (SEO).
Global Error Tracking: You use Winston for logging, but in production, you need a service like Sentry or LogRocket to alert you the moment a user hits a 500 error.
Payment Webhooks: Your payment verification currently happens in the request-response cycle. If the user's browser closes before the verification call completes, the order remains "Pending" even if they paid.
Fix: Implement a Razorpay Webhook to listen for payment.captured events directly from the gateway.
Infrastructure Security:
Add Rate Limiting to the /api/test and /api/products routes (not just auth).
Implement SSL/TLS Enforcement (HSTS) in Helmet.
